# f1 = count, f2 = weigh, f3 = turn . L0 = Span
# `span: Span` is written in a checked file, and the one caller hands `count` numbers out of an `any[]`: the guard at its entry tested for L0, failed at every call, and behind a failing
# guard stands the whole function written straight (133,518 instructions a turn of a hundred calls against 5,655). Every caller of `count` is known, and Link has PROVEN what arrives:
# undefined|i32|L0. Where a number, a text or a boolean is proven to arrive beside the objects and the body does not tell them apart, the guard does not test that parameter.
# `weigh` has left for unseen code: nothing is proven of what arrives, and the written word is tested for as before.
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: function f1 
# CHECK: parameter 1 expected=undefined|null|L0 declared proven=undefined|i32|L0
# RUN(PLAN): plan units mechanisms=all
# PLAN: unit f1:GenericCallEntry -> f1:Body
# PLAN-NOT: unit f1:ParameterGuard
# PLAN: unit f2:ParameterGuard (JSValue, JSValue) -> (Double) tests (-, L0)
